# A rename that waits for the owners of the files it relinks is not closed by another
# extension's request (#269). tests/drive.rs installs a csv-table that takes six seconds to
# answer file/edit for a rename to Rakata, and the open-tasks example patched to send
# workspace/open for Krakatoa when another program writes an eighteenth task. The dialog
# stays, the status line says what was not done, and when the owner answers the rename is
# made: tests/drive.rs checks the note is Rakata.md.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
env COLD_LAVA_TODAY=2026-11-07
wait-for ☐ 17 open tasks
keys /
type krakatoa
wait-for Krakatoa
keys enter
wait-for ← Eruptions.csv  Krakatoa 1883 6
keys R
wait-for rename · ⏎ preview · Esc cancel
keys ctrl+u
type Rakata
keys enter
wait-for Volcanoes/Krakatoa.md  →  Volcanoes/Rakata.md
keys enter
wait-for waiting for csv-table to update its files · Esc cancel
write Inbox/Chores.md - [ ] Sweep the ash off the roof\n
wait-for ☐ 18 open tasks
wait-for open-tasks wanted to open Volcanoes/Krakatoa.md: not while a rename waits for its files' owners
expect waiting for csv-table to update its files · Esc cancel
screen
wait-for 15s renamed to Volcanoes/Rakata.md
keys q
exits 0
